# ===== Toolchain / vendored binaries (installed locally, never tracked) =====
# Root-anchored only: a bare "tools/" also matched the Kotlin package
# src/closepaw/app/src/main/kotlin/ai/closepaw/voice/tools/ and silently dropped the
# whole device-capability layer from the repo.
/tools/
# Nested snapshot (src/closepaw) keeps its toolchain binaries here too, but its
# `tools/termux-bridge/` is *source*: `app/build.gradle.kts` `copyClosePawBridge` copies
# `tools/termux-bridge/closepaw_bridge.py` into `res/raw/` at `preBuild`. Excluding the
# directory itself would drop the bridge source and leave a clean checkout unbuildable
# (git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded), so the rule is
# content-level with an explicit exception.
/src/closepaw/tools/*
!/src/closepaw/tools/termux-bridge/
/sdk_tmp/

